  "instructions": [
    "In a large claypot, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add the onion and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the caraway seeds and smoked paprika, and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the pinto beans, crushed tomatoes, vegetable broth, apple cider vinegar, brown sugar, salt, and black pepper. Stir to combine.",
    "Add the bay leaves and water to the pot.",
    "Bring the stew to a simmer, then reduce the heat to low and cook, covered, for 25-30 minutes, or until the beans are tender.",
    "Stir in the smoked chipotle peppers in adobo sauce and cook for an additional 5 minutes.",
    "Garnish with chopped parsley and chives, and serve hot.",
    "Serve the stew hot, garnished with additional parsley and chives, if desired.",
    "Strain the stew through a fine-mesh sieve to remove the bay leaves before serving, if desired."
  ],
